title: 'statement-store: move the v2 DHT path to statement/3'
doc:
- audience: [Node Operator, Node Dev]
  description: |-
    A node with `--statement-v2-dht` now speaks `statement/3` and falls back to `statement/2`
    and `statement/1`. A node without the flag does not change. The negotiated protocol tells
    whether a peer runs the DHT path: a full peer that falls back to `statement/2` floods, so it
    gets every statement from the moment it connects, without the ten second wait for its
    affinity filter.
    Nodes that run the flag reach each other over the DHT only when both run this change. A node
    with the flag on an older build is served as a flood peer.
    The counters `substrate_sync_statement_peers_assumed_match_all_total` and
    `substrate_sync_statement_late_affinity_filters_total` are removed.
crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
